{{!-- What one dice-rolling step of a Seasons Change move DID to Surplus — an AppliedStepRoll,
      passed as the context.

      Rendered in two places off the one partial: on the sheet, under the step that rolled it, and on
      the roll's own chat card, which used to report the dice and say nothing about the number they
      had just moved. Same record, same words, so the card and the sheet cannot come to disagree
      about what a season cost. --}}
<p class="stonetop-applied">
	<span class="stonetop-applied-what">
		{{localize labelKey amount=amount from=from to=to}}
	</span>
	{{!-- What was OWED, where that is worth saying: because the steading could not pay it, or
	      because an improvement made it something other than what the dice said. Never both —
	      being short is the more urgent of the two, and it names the same number. --}}
	{{#if wasShort}}
		<span class="stonetop-applied-short">
			{{localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.steps.applied.short" due=due}}
		</span>
		{{!-- Named, not merely implied by the shortfall: the move's own words send the table to the
		      Disaster, and the line that records the shortfall is where a reader is looking. Plain
		      text — the step's prose above already renders the linked reference. --}}
		<span class="stonetop-applied-disaster">
			{{localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.steps.applied.disaster"}}
		</span>
	{{else if wasAdjusted}}
		<span class="stonetop-applied-rolled">
			{{localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.steps.applied.rolled" total=total}}
		</span>
	{{/if}}
</p>
